      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's definitely better than the draft. i think it's okay, but the clarity on the actual steps is still a bit vague for a dev who just wants to know how to implement it. \n\ncould you do one more pass? try to make it more of a \"quick start\" style guide where the steps are explicit. also, i just checked the coverage score on this version and we're at a 0.8. management is already asking why we haven't hit 1.0 on this module yet. \n\ncan you refine the instructions to be more actionable while making sure we get that 1.0 coverage score? just please keep it readable—i really don't want to have to fix any weird \"keyword stuffing\" if they flag it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
